```

Careful: the file may be new — `content` given and file not present on base. Then mode is 100644. Also the twin might exist even though the .github file doesn't? E.g. self/atomaton/skills/x.md exists but .github/atomaton/skills/x.md doesn't — the self-overlay test forbids that ("every file in self/ has a counterpart in .github/"). Anyway, handle: twin read from base.

Also: if the .github path exists and has no twin → stage only .github side; report.

Also PR base: `base` from fetchBaseTip.

For the PR body: `baseEditPrBody` plus agent's own `body` appended. The body must not carry PARENT_ISSUE_TAG: don't call injectParentIssue. But we should refuse command lines and check mentions and refuse closing keywords. Also should the version in the body include `Opened by` line? `openedByLine` writes `Opened by` — this drives who the review sends back to. Since this PR has no parent issue, `validate_pull_request` reads ORIGIN_AGENT_TAG for `engineerAgent` — the mention. Should we write ORIGIN_AGENT_TAG? `ORIGIN_AGENT_TAG` is read as `engineerAgent` and used for `askFor` naming. It also is read by `dispatch_post_merge` (with no parent → nothing). And `notify_pr_rejected` reads ORIGIN_AGENT_TAG with issueNumber empty → `no-parent` → nothing.

