Wait — there's another thing: the review route on a PR run. When the reviewer requests changes, the reviewed PR run is the reviewer, and the fix goes to `ORIGIN_AGENT_TAG.readProse` → engineer. That run is on the PR node with a branch that is `atomaton/amend-...`. The engineer would commit_and_push to that branch — `branchForCommit` resolves from the PR's head branch... Let me check `branchForCommit`: for a PR run, it checks out the head branch. That works: the engineer resumes the amend branch and fixes. Good.

Now: dispatch validation with an ask comment. We post a comment on the new PR (llm-context=exclude) to get the ask id. Use `commentOnWithId` from work-tree.ts (that's exactly the helper). Note comment-read-sites allows `work-tree.ts`.

